## :Hover

Preview whatever the cursor is resting on, and switch the parts of it on and off

| Invocation | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `:Hover images [{state}]` | whether pictures and rasterized PDF pages are drawn into the float |
| `:Hover links [{state}]` | whether a target written with link syntax hovers at all |
| `:Hover links web [{state}]` | whether http(s) links hover (off by default: documentation is made of links) |
| `:Hover links web fetch [{state}]` | fetch a hovered link for its status code and page title (implies `links web on`) |
| `:Hover mode [{mode}]` | Set the mode: auto opens by itself, manual only on request, off not at all |
| `:Hover office [{state}]` | render office documents through a PDF instead of showing a badge |
| `:Hover paths [{state}]` | whether a path written in prose or a comment hovers |
| `:Hover paths code [{state}]` | whether a bare path hovers inside executable code, not just comments and strings |
| `:Hover paths missing [{state}]` | whether a bare path that resolves to nothing is reported as broken |
| `:Hover pin` | Keep this hover on screen while the cursor goes elsewhere |
| `:Hover positions [{state}]` | whether a plugin may say something about a cursor position that points at nothing |
| `:Hover show` | Show the hover for whatever is under the cursor, ignoring every volume switch |
| `:Hover status` | Report the mode and every switch in one message |
| `:Hover toggle` | Turn the hover off for this session, or back on |
| `:Hover why` | Say why nothing hovered at the cursor |

`{mode}` ∈ `auto | manual | off`  
`{state}` ∈ `on | off | toggle`  
